      "title": "Why synapses alone are insufficient",
      "gist": "Traditional models built only on spikes and synaptic connections cannot plausibly implement such fast control, since they would require the system to track exactly which synapses to coordinate in real time, suggesting brain wave oscillations play a complementary coordinating role."
    },
