      "title": "20th century neuroscience: The classical model of neural information processing",
      "gist": "Classical connectionist models of fixed, specialized neurons cannot explain findings like widespread multifunctional neural coding, motivating a search for additional mechanisms.",
      "question": "The connectionist model — why does it fail to explain how cortical neurons actually encode information? (an empirical anomaly)",
      "sourceHeading": "20th century neuroscience: The classical model of neural information processing"
