      "title": "20th century neuroscience: The classical model of neural information processing",
      "gist": "Classical connectionist models describe hierarchical, feedforward circuits where each neuron has one stable, specialized function, but this account, while useful for sensory cortex, cannot explain why any task engages about a third of prefrontal neurons at once.",
      "sourceHeading": "20th century neuroscience: The classical model of neural information processing"
