      "title": "Oscillatory control and spatial computing",
      "gist": "Brain wave oscillations can directly and rapidly shape spiking through electric field effects, and a 'Spatial Computing' theory explains how alpha/beta waves route information to produce mixed selectivity and organized population coding.",
      "question": "Brain waves — how could they flexibly route information among overlapping neural populations? (a mechanistic theory)"
    },
    "n0040": {
      "id": "n0040",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0039",
