      "title": "Oscillations directly influence spiking via ephaptic coupling",
      "gist": "Electric fields generated by neural activity can influence nearby neurons' spiking without synapses, a process called ephaptic coupling, which is fast, spreads across millimeters, and can coordinate large neural populations more efficiently than synaptic signaling alone.",
      "sourceHeading": "Oscillations directly influence spiking via ephaptic coupling"
