      "title": "Explaining mixed selectivity with spatial computing",
      "gist": "Because overlapping alpha/beta stencils gate the same neurons differently across contexts, a single neuron's effective selectivity can change with context, mechanistically explaining nonlinear mixed selectivity without requiring dedicated context-coding neurons.",
      "sourceHeading": "Explaining mixed selectivity with spatial computing"
