      "title": "Traveling Waves and Representational Change",
      "gist": "Brain waves often sweep across cortex as traveling waves, and alpha/beta and theta traveling waves may drive transitions between different neural coding states underlying perception, memory, and action.",
      "question": "Traveling waves — how might moving wave patterns, not just standing oscillations, transition the brain between different states of neural coding? (a proposed mechanism)",
      "sourceHeading": "Traveling Waves and Representational Change"
    },
