      "title": "Traveling waves and beta's role in motor and memory states",
      "gist": "Brain waves frequently travel across the cortical surface at speeds consistent with long-range horizontal connections, and beta traveling waves in motor and prefrontal cortex appear at moments when neural representations are newly forming or transforming."
    },
