      ],
      "title": "Analog computing through wave superposition",
      "gist": "Analog computing uses continuous physical quantities rather than binary signals, and when brain waves meet they add, cancel, or interfere, offering a physical basis for parallel computations like addition and filtering of neural information."
    },
