      "title": "A Hybrid Synapse/Wave Framework for Cognition and Consciousness",
      "gist": "Anesthesia and theoretical comparisons support a hybrid framework in which synapses store information while coordinated wave dynamics, not synaptic change, drive moment-to-moment cognition and may give rise to consciousness.",
      "question": "Cognition and consciousness — how do synapses and brain waves jointly explain them, and how does this compare to other theories? (a synthesis and comparison)"
    },
